# Figures and tables: script map

Every figure and table of the paper is produced by a script in `figures/scripts/` from the result files in `code/results/` (written by the code in `code/`). The scripts never recompute a statistic: ratios, intervals, biases and ordering accuracies come from `code/results/*.csv` (the file names below); the scripts only select rows, pool across benchmarks by the rule stated in each script's docstring, and format. No number is typed by hand.

**Run everything:** `sh figures/scripts/make_all.sh [CODE_DIR]` from the root of the delivered paper (`CODE_DIR` defaults to `code/`; it must contain `results/`). It writes `figures/*.pdf` and `tables/*.tex`; about 40 s on one CPU. Needs Python 3 with numpy, pandas and matplotlib (versions: `code/requirements.txt`). Shared style (venue text width 5.5 in; tick and legend text at least 7 pt, titles at least 8 pt; Type 42 fonts; one fixed style per method class): `figures/scripts/style.py`; which methods are shown and how they are named: `figures/scripts/common.py`.

